## Test Anti-Pattern Audit: `ProductCatalogTests.cs`

**Summary: 10 tests, 8 Critical findings, 2 Medium — this suite is almost entirely coverage theater.**

Every public method on `ProductCatalog` is called (hence 95% coverage), but almost nothing is actually verified. Bugs in pricing, search, CSV export/import, and removal would all pass these tests silently.

---

### 🔴 CRITICAL

#### 1. Coverage-Touching Pattern (Systemic)
**Lines 6–89 — the entire class**

The suite methodically calls all 9 public methods in declaration order. Of the 10 tests, **5 have zero assertions** and **4 use only `Assert.IsNotNull`** — a trivially-true check on methods that always return non-null (empty list / empty string). This is the textbook coverage-touching pattern.

#### 2. No Assertions (5 tests)

| Test | Line | What it misses |
|---|---|---|
| `AddProduct_Works` | 17 | Never verifies the product was actually stored |
| `UpdatePrice_Works` | 32 | Never checks the price changed from 9.99 → 14.99 |
| `RemoveProduct_Works` | 38 | Never checks the product is actually gone |
| `GetProductCount_Works` | 63 | Calls `GetProductCount()`, discards the result entirely |
| `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works` | 68 | Never checks that prices were reduced by 10% |
| `ImportFromCsv_Works` | 85 | Never checks that the product was imported |

**Fix — example for `AddProduct_Works`:**
```csharp
// BEFORE (line 17)
[TestMethod]
public void AddProduct_Works()
{
    var product = new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m);
    _catalog.AddProduct(product);
}

// AFTER
[TestMethod]
public void AddProduct_StoresProduct()
{
    var product = new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m);
    _catalog.AddProduct(product);

    var retrieved = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
    Assert.AreEqual("Widget", retrieved?.Name);
    Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, retrieved?.Price);
}
```

**Fix — `UpdatePrice_Works`:**
```csharp
// AFTER
[TestMethod]
public void UpdatePrice_ChangesStoredPrice()
{
    _catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
    _catalog.UpdatePrice("SKU-001", 14.99m);

    var updated = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
    Assert.AreEqual(14.99m, updated?.Price);
}
```

**Fix — `RemoveProduct_Works`:**
```csharp
// AFTER
[TestMethod]
public void RemoveProduct_ProductNoLongerRetrievable()
{
    _catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
    _catalog.RemoveProduct("SKU-001");

    Assert.IsNull(_catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001"));
}
```

